Your diagram shows an **end-to-end Digital Intelligence AI Platform** with clear separation of layers: UI, security, runtime services, LLM gateway, data/vector storage, governance, and deployment.

## What I understand from your architecture

You are building a platform where users interact through a **web application**. The request enters through a secure access layer, then gets routed into either:

**1. Chatbot / Agent service**
For conversational AI, RAG, task execution, and user interaction.

**2. AI Insights / Reporting service**
For generating analytical insights, summaries, reports, dashboards, and possibly PDF/email outputs.

The platform uses an **LLM Gateway** as the central control point for prompts, safety, routing, model selection, quality checks, and cost control. Data comes from object storage, OLTP/cache systems, and enterprise data warehouses such as Snowflake or Databricks. Vector search supports RAG. Observability, audit, governance, and CI/CD sit underneath the platform.

